## The standard (fixed — do not localize)

How to build, test, debug, and ship on CkFoundation is defined by:

1. The **ck-game-\* skill set** (junctioned into `.claude/skills/` by sync-skills):
   ck-game-project-bootstrap, ck-game-feature-recipe, ck-game-angelscript-gameplay,
   ck-game-entity-composition-patterns, ck-game-driver-architecture,
   ck-game-replication-patterns, ck-game-debugging-playbook, ck-game-testing-discipline,
   ck-game-build-and-cook, ck-game-framework-boundary.
2. The **framework doc chain**: `Plugins/CkFoundation/CLAUDE.md` (doctrine + skill index),
   `Plugins/CkFoundation/Source/CLAUDE.md` (module decision tree), `Plugins/CkFoundation/Script/CLAUDE.md`
   (AngelScript language), `Plugins/CkTests/CLAUDE.md` (test pipelines + spec trust levels).

Questions about skills, patterns, or doctrine are answered THERE, not here. If this file
and a framework doc disagree, the framework doc wins for anything generic; this file wins
only for the per-project facts it owns — and the conflict itself is a bug: fix whichever
is stale, or record a dated entry under **Intentional divergences**.

**sync-skills ritual:** after every framework-submodule update, run
`Plugins/CkFoundation/.claude/scripts/sync-skills.ps1` from the repo root. The first-ever
creation of `.claude/skills/` requires a Claude session restart to be picked up.

